1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Translators' Note

2
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:16,480
What shall we talk about?

3
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:24,480
What do you think is the most important thing

4
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:28,480
that we three can talk about?

5
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:31,480
Well, the one thing... I've had an idea lately,

6
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:34,480
and there's one thing that's been on my mind,

7
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:37,480
and I've been getting it from when we talked before,

8
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:41,480
and that is there's a feeling you've been conveying

9
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:47,480
that life comes first and not thought or work.

10
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,480
Something like that. In other

11
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,480
words, that I find in myself,

12
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,480
and I find I think that most

13
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:57,480
people are caught up in the fact that...

14
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:58,480
You know, you said once,

15
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:00,480
we live second-hand lives.

16
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:02,480
If we could talk about that, I think,

17
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:06,479
the second-handness of our life.

18
00:01:06,479 --> 00:01:08,479
What do you mean?

19
00:01:08,479 --> 00:01:11,479
Well, in relation to that,

20
00:01:11,479 --> 00:01:13,979
I perhaps would like to

21
00:01:13,979 --> 00:01:16,479
talk about the question of wholeness.

22
00:01:16,479 --> 00:01:18,479
Yes, of wholeness.

23
00:01:18,479 --> 00:01:20,479
Shall we talk about that first?

24
00:01:20,479 --> 00:01:21,479
Which first?

25
00:01:21,479 --> 00:01:22,479
And then include yours.

26
00:01:22,479 --> 00:01:24,479
Sure. I mean, I think this is part of it.

27
00:01:24,479 --> 00:01:27,479
I see that the second-handness is not wholeness.

28
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:32,480
I wonder how we can approach this question.

29
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:43,480
Knowing that most people are fragmented, broken up,

30
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,480
and not whole,

31
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:53,480
how do we tackle or approach this question?

32
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:59,480
Through direct awareness of the fragmentation.

33
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:03,480
No, I would like to... I'm just asking because...

34
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:08,479
Are we discussing it theoretically?

35
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:10,479
No.

36
00:02:10,479 --> 00:02:12,480
Verbally?

37
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:17,480
Or taking ourselves, you, we three,

38
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:19,480
taking ourselves as we are,

39
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:22,480
and examining what we mean by fragmented?

40
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,480
Right.

41
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:27,480
And then work from there what is the whole,

42
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:30,480
not theoretically or verbally.

43
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,480
Right.

44
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:34,480
Then I think that has vitality, that has some meaning.

45
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,480
Right, right.

46
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:38,480
Well, if we see the fragmentation, the wholeness is there.

47
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:39,480
No, no.

48
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:40,480
Or will it be there?

49
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:42,480
Don't assume anything.

50
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:43,480
Oh, that's right.

51
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:44,480
That's too fast.

52
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:45,480
Then we are off to theory.

53
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:47,480
Okay. Right, right.

54
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,480
You know, we've been talking,

55
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:56,480
there are a lot of students here, this question.

56
00:02:56,480 --> 00:03:00,480
Dr Bohm was there too.

57
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:04,980
And whether we can ever

58
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:09,480
be aware of ourselves at all.

59
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:19,480
Or we are only aware of patches,

60
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:23,480
not the totality of fragmentations.

61
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:26,480
I don't know if I am conveying this.

62
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:28,480
Well, you can. Go ahead.

63
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:30,480
Yes.

64
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:35,480
Can one be aware, conscious, know,

65
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:39,480
the various fragments?

66
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:46,480
Or examining one by one by one by one,

67
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,480
and who is the examiner?

68
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:53,480
Is he also a fragment,

69
00:03:53,480 --> 00:03:56,480
who has assumed an authority?

70
00:03:56,480 --> 00:04:04,480
So when we talk about being aware of fragments,

71
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:12,480
socially, morally, ethically, religiously, business, art,

72
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:15,480
you know, the whole activity is fragmented.

73
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:17,480
Is one aware of fragments?

74
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:22,480
Is one aware of the movement of these fragments?

75
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,480
Yes.

76
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:29,480
Or do you take one fragment and examine it?

77
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:32,480
Or say, yes, I am aware of that,

78
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,480
and not the many.

79
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,480
You follow what I am saying?

80
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,480
I am following you.

81
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:41,480
I think you are mostly aware of...

82
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,480
I seem to...

83
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:44,480
When I think of what you are saying,

84
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,980
I seem to be aware

85
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:47,480
of a kind of many fragments.

86
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,480
Are you?

87
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:51,480
Well, not one at a time, you know,

88
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:54,480
spread it like that, like a machine gun.

89
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:57,480
Yes. So you are really aware one by one.

90
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,480
Right.

91
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:01,480
And caught up by the movement of the fragments.

92
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:04,480
One by one. Is that so?

93
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:07,480
Are you sure that it is so?

94
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:15,480
Yes. I think, I mean, it seems to be that...

95
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:18,480
Well, then sometimes you can take a step back,

96
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,480
or you seem to take a step back,

97
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:22,480
or I seem to take a step back,

98
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,480
and I am aware of these many.

99
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,480
No, when Dr. Worm asked,

100
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,480
can't we talk over together

101
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:33,480
this question of wholeness,

102
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:39,480
which implies holiness, health, sanity, and all that,

103
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:44,480
I wonder from what source he is asking that question.

104
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:49,480
Yes. You mean, is he coming from a fragmented position,

105
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,480
or is he coming from a whole position?

106
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:54,480
No, no, if he is asking from the whole position,

107
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:57,480
there is no question.

108
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:05,480
So I would like to, if one may ask,

109
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:10,480
are we aware of the fragments as a whole,

110
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:13,480
a collection of fragments,

111
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:20,480
or are we aware of one fragment at each time?

112
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:23,480
What do you say, sir?

113
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:27,480
Well, in general, the thing presents itself first

114
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:29,480
as primarily one fragment...

115
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,480
One fragment at a time.

116
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,480
...with a background of all the other fragments,

117
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,480
perhaps dimly present.

118
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:39,480
I mean, in the beginning,

119
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:42,480
that one fragment seems to take emphasis

120
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:46,480
or preeminence in awareness.

121
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:50,480
Doesn't that one fragment fragment out quickly

122
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:53,480
into many little fragments?

123
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:55,480
I have an idea,

124
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:59,480
and then that idea is in contrast to another idea,

125
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:02,480
so I'm immediately caught up into two fragments there.

126
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:05,480
And then I have another idea,

127
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:09,480
which is the repetition of that first idea,

128
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,480
so I'm caught up in a movement of fragments,

129
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:13,480
rather than...

130
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,480
I mean, my attitude is fragmented,

131
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:17,480
my relationship is fragmented,

132
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:21,480
my very substance of movement

133
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:23,480
is a feeling of fragmentation.

134
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:26,480
I don't have any center when I'm fragmented.

135
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:28,480
I'm not...

136
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,480
I'm not sure about that.

137
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,480
That's a question.

138
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:32,480
I'm not at all sure...

139
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:34,480
No, no.

140
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,480
...that there is no center when you're fragmented.

141
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:38,480
Well, I think definitely there is a center.

142
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,480
There is.

143
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,480
I mean, that is the major fragment you're aware of.

144
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,480
The major fragment, that's right.

145
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:43,480
I mean, that...

146
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:48,480
Then let's go into that more.

147
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:51,480
Well, I just think that there is a center

148
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:54,480
which you may sense anywhere,

149
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,480
say here or here.

150
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,480
Yeah.

151
00:07:56,480 --> 00:08:00,480
And that seems to be the center of everything, right?

152
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:03,480
Everything that's connected to everything, right?

153
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,480
Well, I see what you're saying,

154
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:08,480
but I feel that when the fragmentation is going on,

155
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:10,480
it's like the center is looking for

156
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,480
itself.

157
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,480
It feels like it's not a center.

158
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:14,480
Are you aware of the fragmentation?

159
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:17,480
Not fragmentation is going on.

160
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:18,480
No, you're not.

161
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,480
I'm not.

162
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:24,480
Then what are we aware of?

163
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:27,480
I think that's a terrific question,

164
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:30,480
because I think when there's fragmentation,

165
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:33,480
what we're aware of is like being sucked forward

166
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:35,480
into more fragments.

167
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,480
In other words, there's a kind of movement

168
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,480
of more fragmentation, more fragmentation,

169
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:43,480
more fragmentation, which is what we're aware of.

170
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:47,480
It's what you've talked about in terms of pleasure.

171
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:49,480
It's like pleasure is pulling us forward

172
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,480
into more fragments.

173
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:51,480
This would give me pleasure.

174
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,480
That would give me pleasure.

175
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:54,480
That would give me pleasure.

176
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:56,480
And it's that feeling of pieces.

177
00:08:56,480 --> 00:09:00,480
Before we go into the question of pleasure,

178
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:06,480
are we aware actually from a center

179
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:08,480
which says, I am fragmented?

180
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:15,480
That is the question, isn't it?

181
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,480
Right, that's the question.

182
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,480
Well, we're both aware of a center

183
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:21,480
and from a center, you say.

184
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,480
That's it.

185
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:25,480
And this center seems to be, as you say,

186
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:28,480
the fragment that is dominating

187
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:30,480
or attempting to dominate.

188
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,480
That center is the dominating factor.

189
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,480
Yes.

190
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:36,480
Which is in itself a fragment.

191
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,480
Yes, I mean, this center is itself...

192
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:41,480
Well, it seems to be the center of your being,

193
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,480
as it were, the center

194
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:45,480
of the ego or the self,

195
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:49,480
which one might think is the whole.

196
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:50,480
Quite, quite.

197
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:53,480
Because it's in contact with everything, you see.

198
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,480
In other words...

199
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:58,480
Would you say having a center

200
00:09:58,480 --> 00:10:01,480
is the very cause of fragmentation?

201
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,480
Yes, I would say that, although at first sight

202
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,480
it seems quite different to me.

203
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:06,480
At first sight it seems...

204
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,480
And I think that's important,

205
00:10:07,480 --> 00:10:08,480
the difference between it.

206
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,480
At first sight it doesn't seem that way.

207
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:12,480
Well, at first sight it seems that the center

208
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:15,480
is what is organizing everything into a whole.

209
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:16,480
Right.

210
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,480
Yes.

211
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:18,480
In other words, one feels one wants a center

212
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,480
to bring everything to a whole,

213
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:22,480
to stop the fragmentation.

214
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,480
Yes, try to bring about integration,

215
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,480
try to...

216
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,480
Wholeness, yes.

217
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:27,480
Wholeness and all that.

218
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,480
Right, if you feel the fragmentation

219
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:31,480
and then you center here and you say,

220
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:33,480
I can see all the fragmentations,

221
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,480
but that's still center.

222
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:36,480
No, but I'm asking whether

223
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,480
when there is a center,

224
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:41,480
doesn't it make for fragments?

225
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,480
That I see.

226
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,480
I see what you're saying,

227
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:45,480
but I'm trying to take it from the...

228
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:50,480
What is the experience when there is fragmentation?

229
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,480
There doesn't seem to be a center.

230
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,480
A contradiction.

231
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:55,480
Right.

232
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:57,480
But it doesn't feel like a center.

233
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,480
No, contradiction.

234
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:01,480
So when there are fragments,

235
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:03,480
I am aware of the fragments

236
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:05,480
because of contradiction.

237
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,480
Because of...

238
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:09,480
Because opposing factors.

239
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:12,480
You mean by contradiction also conflict.

240
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,480
Conflict, yes.

241
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:16,480
Out of contradiction there is conflict.

242
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:19,480
Then I'm aware that there are fragments.

243
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:22,480
I'm working in an area of fragments.

244
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:24,480
Right.

245
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:26,480
But then, yes,

246
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:28,480
and then I'm not aware of the fact

247
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:32,480
that I have in fact got a center.

248
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,480
That's the self-deception right there.

249
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:38,480
No, I think, don't you think,

250
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:40,480
if I may suggest,

251
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:46,480
that where there is conflict,

252
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:49,480
then only you are aware

253
00:11:50,114 --> 00:11:50,914
で

254
00:11:50,914 --> 00:11:55,914
aware of a conflict, of contradiction.

255
00:11:55,914 --> 00:12:02,474
That is, one is aware only when there is conflict.

256
00:12:02,474 --> 00:12:04,974
Right?

257
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:12,034
And then the next awareness, the next movement is...

258
00:12:12,034 --> 00:12:15,794
conflict arises out of conflict,

259
00:12:15,794 --> 00:12:18,974
conflict arises out of fragmentation,

260
00:12:18,974 --> 00:12:21,213
opposing elements, opposing desires,

261
00:12:21,213 --> 00:12:26,214
opposing wishes, opposing thoughts.

262
00:12:26,214 --> 00:12:28,594
But are you saying that these

263
00:12:28,594 --> 00:12:30,974
oppose first before one is aware,

264
00:12:30,974 --> 00:12:34,094
and then suddenly you are aware through the unpleasantness

265
00:12:34,094 --> 00:12:35,834
or the pain of the

266
00:12:35,834 --> 00:12:37,574
opposition, that the conflict is unpleasant?

267
00:12:37,574 --> 00:12:39,674
Yes, conflict is unpleasant and

268
00:12:39,674 --> 00:12:41,774
therefore one is aware that...

269
00:12:41,774 --> 00:12:47,214
That something is wrong. Wrong. Yes.

270
00:12:47,214 --> 00:12:48,974
Yes, or something is wrong,

271
00:12:48,974 --> 00:12:50,974
not just simply wrong, but wrong with the whole thing.

272
00:12:50,974 --> 00:12:54,734
Whole thing, of course.

273
00:12:54,734 --> 00:12:58,974
Sir, after all, self-consciousness,

274
00:12:58,974 --> 00:13:01,094
when you are aware of

275
00:13:01,094 --> 00:13:03,214
yourself only when there is pain,

276
00:13:03,214 --> 00:13:06,654
or intense pleasure.

277
00:13:06,654 --> 00:13:11,694
Otherwise you are not aware of yourself.

278
00:13:11,694 --> 00:13:12,534
Right.

279
00:13:12,534 --> 00:13:18,734
So fragmentation with its conflict

280
00:13:18,734 --> 00:13:22,074
brings this sense of, I

281
00:13:22,074 --> 00:13:25,414
am aware, I am in conflict.

282
00:13:25,414 --> 00:13:27,734
Otherwise there is no awareness.

283
00:13:27,734 --> 00:13:28,613
I wonder if I am...

284
00:13:28,613 --> 00:13:30,574
Yes, go ahead.

285
00:13:30,574 --> 00:13:34,773
You are saying that the very fragmentation itself

286
00:13:34,773 --> 00:13:36,574
breeds the centre.

287
00:13:36,574 --> 00:13:37,854
Breeds the centre.

288
00:13:37,854 --> 00:13:39,473
And the centre has bred the

289
00:13:39,473 --> 00:13:41,093
fragmentation, so it is like a...

290
00:13:41,093 --> 00:13:42,414
Yes, back and forth.

291
00:13:42,414 --> 00:13:42,934
Right.

292
00:13:42,934 --> 00:13:44,773
Well, I mean, would you

293
00:13:44,773 --> 00:13:46,613
say that the thought in itself

294
00:13:46,613 --> 00:13:48,734
before there is a centre breeds conflict?

295
00:13:48,734 --> 00:13:49,734
Yes, I mean...

296
00:13:49,734 --> 00:13:50,734
Thought...

297
00:13:50,734 --> 00:13:52,734
Or is there a thought before a centre?

298
00:13:52,734 --> 00:13:54,734
Is there... Oh, thought before the centre.

299
00:13:54,734 --> 00:13:56,734
Yes.

300
00:13:56,734 --> 00:13:58,234
I mean, one view is to

301
00:13:58,234 --> 00:13:59,734
say that the centre and thought

302
00:13:59,734 --> 00:14:02,734
are always co-existent and one breeds the other.

303
00:14:02,734 --> 00:14:03,734
One breeds the other, quite right.

304
00:14:03,734 --> 00:14:05,234
Or the other view is to

305
00:14:05,234 --> 00:14:06,734
say that there might be thought first

306
00:14:06,734 --> 00:14:10,734
and that produces conflict and then that produces a centre.

307
00:14:10,734 --> 00:14:14,734
No, let's go into that a little bit.

308
00:14:14,734 --> 00:14:17,734
That's a good one, huh?

309
00:14:18,734 --> 00:14:22,734
Does thought exist before conflict?

310
00:14:22,734 --> 00:14:23,734
Before a centre.

311
00:14:23,734 --> 00:14:25,734
Before the centre.

312
00:14:25,734 --> 00:14:27,734
Which centre only...

313
00:14:27,734 --> 00:14:29,234
One is aware of the

314
00:14:29,234 --> 00:14:30,734
centre only when there is conflict.

315
00:14:30,734 --> 00:14:32,734
Yes, because that comes in apparently

316
00:14:32,734 --> 00:14:34,734
to try to bring about wholeness again.

317
00:14:34,734 --> 00:14:36,734
You see, to take charge of everything.

318
00:14:36,734 --> 00:14:38,734
The centre tries to take

319
00:14:38,734 --> 00:14:40,734
charge or try to create wholeness.

320
00:14:40,734 --> 00:14:43,734
Yes, to bring all the factors together.

321
00:14:43,734 --> 00:14:45,734
But centre itself is a fragment.

322
00:14:45,734 --> 00:14:47,734
Yes, but it doesn't know that.

323
00:14:47,734 --> 00:14:50,234
Of course, it doesn't know, but it

324
00:14:50,234 --> 00:14:52,734
thinks it can bring all the fragments together,

325
00:14:52,734 --> 00:14:54,734
make it a whole.

326
00:14:54,734 --> 00:14:57,734
So Dr. Bohm is asking a question which is,

327
00:14:57,734 --> 00:15:01,734
did thought exist before the centre

328
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:04,734
or the centre existed before the thought?

329
00:15:04,734 --> 00:15:06,734
Or the two together.

330
00:15:06,734 --> 00:15:07,734
Or the two together.

331
00:15:07,734 --> 00:15:09,734
Right, right.

332
00:15:09,734 --> 00:15:12,734
Or he's also asking, does thought create the centre?

333
00:15:12,734 --> 00:15:14,734
Thought creates the centre.

334
00:15:14,734 --> 00:15:16,734
That would be the action, the very creation

335
00:15:16,734 --> 00:15:17,734
in the...

336
00:15:17,734 --> 00:15:20,734
I mean, sort of an after effect of the thought.

337
00:15:20,734 --> 00:15:23,734
In other words, is the organism...

338
00:15:23,734 --> 00:15:27,234
is the production of thought

339
00:15:27,234 --> 00:15:30,734
the very cause of a centre?

340
00:15:30,734 --> 00:15:32,734
That I think carries it...

341
00:15:32,734 --> 00:15:33,734
Are you asking...

342
00:15:33,734 --> 00:15:35,734
Yes, let's be clear on this point too.

343
00:15:35,734 --> 00:15:36,734
Are you asking...

344
00:15:36,734 --> 00:15:40,734
Are we asking, did thought create the centre?

345
00:15:40,734 --> 00:15:42,234
Yes, and there was therefore a

346
00:15:42,234 --> 00:15:43,734
kind of thought before a centre.

347
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:45,734
Yes, thought before the centre. That's it.

348
00:15:45,734 --> 00:15:46,734
Which came into contradiction.

349
00:15:46,734 --> 00:15:49,734
Yes. Thought created...

350
00:15:49,734 --> 00:15:51,734
Did the thought create the centre

351
00:15:51,734 --> 00:15:54,734
or the centre existed before the thought?

352
00:15:54,734 --> 00:15:55,734
Right.

353
00:15:55,734 --> 00:15:57,734
Or else the centre was...

354
00:15:57,734 --> 00:15:58,734
That's a view which is common.

355
00:15:58,734 --> 00:16:00,234
I mean, people think the

356
00:16:00,234 --> 00:16:01,734
centre is me who was first.

357
00:16:01,734 --> 00:16:02,734
Me is the first.

358
00:16:02,734 --> 00:16:04,734
Then I began to think, right?

359
00:16:04,734 --> 00:16:05,734
Yes.

360
00:16:05,734 --> 00:16:06,734
Or...

361
00:16:06,734 --> 00:16:10,734
No, I think thought exists before the centre.

362
00:16:10,734 --> 00:16:11,734
Yes.

363
00:16:11,734 --> 00:16:12,734
Then we have to ask the question,

364
00:16:12,734 --> 00:16:13,734
and I don't know if we want

365
00:16:13,734 --> 00:16:14,734
to get into it at this minute,

366
00:16:14,734 --> 00:16:15,734
but then we have to ask the question of

367
00:16:15,734 --> 00:16:17,734
why is there thought?

368
00:16:17,734 --> 00:16:18,734
Or what is thought?

369
00:16:18,734 --> 00:16:20,734
Oh, that's a different matter.

370
00:16:20,734 --> 00:16:21,734
Right.

371
00:16:21,734 --> 00:16:22,734
Do we go into that?

372
00:16:22,734 --> 00:16:23,734
That might be a long story.

373
00:16:23,734 --> 00:16:24,734
That's a long story.

374
00:16:24,734 --> 00:16:25,734
I don't think that's for now.

375
00:16:25,734 --> 00:16:26,734
Yes.

376
00:16:26,734 --> 00:16:27,734
But we have to get at that.

377
00:16:27,734 --> 00:16:28,734
No, but as we start...

378
00:16:28,734 --> 00:16:30,734
Let's stay with what we started with.

379
00:16:30,734 --> 00:16:31,734
Yes.

380
00:16:31,734 --> 00:16:34,734
We started out asking,

381
00:16:34,734 --> 00:16:38,734
can we talk about the wholeness of life?

382
00:16:38,734 --> 00:16:40,734
Right.

383
00:16:40,734 --> 00:16:45,734
How can one be aware of that wholeness?

384
00:16:45,734 --> 00:16:47,734
If one is fragmented?

385
00:16:47,734 --> 00:16:50,734
That's the next question.

386
00:16:50,734 --> 00:16:51,734
Well...

387
00:16:51,734 --> 00:16:52,734
You can't be aware of the whole

388
00:16:52,734 --> 00:16:55,734
if I'm only looking through a small hole.

389
00:16:55,734 --> 00:16:56,734
Right, right.

390
00:16:56,734 --> 00:16:57,734
Huh?

391
00:16:57,734 --> 00:16:58,734
Right.

392
00:16:58,734 --> 00:17:00,734
But on the other hand,

393
00:17:00,734 --> 00:17:04,733
in actuality, you are the whole.

394
00:17:04,733 --> 00:17:05,733
Ah!

395
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:06,733
That is a theory.

396
00:17:06,733 --> 00:17:07,733
Is it?

397
00:17:07,733 --> 00:17:08,733
That's what...

398
00:17:08,733 --> 00:17:09,733
A supposition, yes.

399
00:17:09,733 --> 00:17:10,733
Of course it is.

400
00:17:10,733 --> 00:17:11,733
When you are fragmented,

401
00:17:11,733 --> 00:17:13,733
how can you assume that you are the whole?

402
00:17:15,733 --> 00:17:19,733
Well, that's a wonderful...

403
00:17:19,733 --> 00:17:22,733
I mean, that's an issue because...

404
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:24,733
How am I to know I'm fragmented?

405
00:17:24,733 --> 00:17:26,733
That's what we are asking.

406
00:17:26,733 --> 00:17:27,733
Yes.

407
00:17:27,733 --> 00:17:30,734
When are you aware that you are fragmented?

408
00:17:30,734 --> 00:17:31,734
Only when there is conflict.

409
00:17:31,734 --> 00:17:33,734
Right.

410
00:17:33,734 --> 00:17:36,734
That's right.

411
00:17:36,734 --> 00:17:38,734
When there are two opposing desires,

412
00:17:38,734 --> 00:17:43,734
opposing elements of movements,

413
00:17:43,734 --> 00:17:44,734
then there is conflict.

414
00:17:44,734 --> 00:17:45,734
And you say,

415
00:17:45,734 --> 00:17:46,734
well, I'm not going to be fragmented.

416
00:17:46,734 --> 00:17:47,734
Then you have pain,

417
00:17:47,734 --> 00:17:48,734
or whatever it is,

418
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:49,734
and then you become conscious.

419
00:17:49,734 --> 00:17:50,734
Right, right.

420
00:17:50,734 --> 00:17:52,734
But at those moments,

421
00:17:52,734 --> 00:17:53,734
it oftentimes happens

422
00:17:53,734 --> 00:17:55,734
that you don't want to let go of the...

423
00:17:55,734 --> 00:17:57,734
I mean, it's like you feel your fragmentation...

424
00:17:57,734 --> 00:17:58,734
No, no, no.

425
00:17:58,734 --> 00:17:59,734
That's a different matter.

426
00:17:59,734 --> 00:18:00,734
That's a different matter.

427
00:18:00,734 --> 00:18:01,734
Right.

428
00:18:01,734 --> 00:18:02,734
What we are asking is,

429
00:18:02,734 --> 00:18:06,734
can the fragment dissolve itself...

430
00:18:06,734 --> 00:18:08,734
Yeah.

431
00:18:08,734 --> 00:18:10,734
Okay.

432
00:18:10,734 --> 00:18:14,734
...and then only it's possible to see the whole?

433
00:18:14,734 --> 00:18:18,734
You cannot be fragmented and then wish for the whole.

434
00:18:18,734 --> 00:18:19,734
Right.

435
00:18:19,734 --> 00:18:20,734
Then it's merely...

436
00:18:20,734 --> 00:18:21,734
All you really know is your fragmentation.

437
00:18:21,734 --> 00:18:22,734
That's all we know.

438
00:18:22,734 --> 00:18:23,734
That's right.

439
00:18:23,734 --> 00:18:24,734
Therefore, let's stick to that...

440
00:18:24,734 --> 00:18:25,734
Okay.

441
00:18:25,734 --> 00:18:27,734
...and not beat around the bush and say,

442
00:18:27,734 --> 00:18:29,734
well, let's talk about the whole

443
00:18:29,734 --> 00:18:31,734
and all the rest of it.

444
00:18:31,734 --> 00:18:32,734
Yes.

445
00:18:32,734 --> 00:18:34,734
I mean, the supposition that there

446
00:18:34,734 --> 00:18:36,734
is a whole may be apparently reasonable,

447
00:18:36,734 --> 00:18:38,734
but as long as you're fragmented...

448
00:18:38,734 --> 00:18:39,734
That's right.

449
00:18:39,734 --> 00:18:40,734
...you could never see it.

450
00:18:40,734 --> 00:18:41,734
Of course.

451
00:18:41,734 --> 00:18:42,734
It would be just an assumption.

452
00:18:42,734 --> 00:18:43,734
Right.

453
00:18:43,734 --> 00:18:46,734
You may think you've experienced it once,

454
00:18:46,734 --> 00:18:48,734
but that's also an assumption because you don't...

455
00:18:48,734 --> 00:18:49,734
That's gone already.

456
00:18:49,734 --> 00:18:50,734
Absolutely.

457
00:18:50,734 --> 00:18:51,734
Quite right.

458
00:18:51,734 --> 00:18:55,734
You know, I wonder if there's not a tremendous pain

459
00:18:55,734 --> 00:18:58,734
or something that goes on

460
00:18:58,734 --> 00:19:01,734
when I'm aware of my fragmentation.

461
00:19:01,734 --> 00:19:04,734
I mean, that's the loneliness somehow or the other.

462
00:19:04,734 --> 00:19:07,734
Look, sir, can you be aware of your fragments?

463
00:19:07,734 --> 00:19:10,734
That you are an American, that I'm a Hindu,

464
00:19:10,734 --> 00:19:12,734
you are a Jew, you are a...

465
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:14,734
a communist, this or...

466
00:19:14,734 --> 00:19:16,734
You just live in that state.

467
00:19:16,734 --> 00:19:18,734
Yes.

468
00:19:18,734 --> 00:19:21,734
You don't say, well, I know I am a Hindu.

469
00:19:21,734 --> 00:19:22,734
You...

470
00:19:22,734 --> 00:19:24,734
It's only when you are challenged.

471
00:19:24,734 --> 00:19:26,734
Mm-hmm.

472
00:19:27,734 --> 00:19:30,734
It's only when you say, what are you?

473
00:19:30,734 --> 00:19:32,734
Then you say, yes, I'm an

474
00:19:32,734 --> 00:19:34,734
Indian or a Hindu or an Arab.

475
00:19:34,734 --> 00:19:36,234
Or when the country is challenged and

476
00:19:36,234 --> 00:19:37,734
you have to go to war, yes.

477
00:19:37,734 --> 00:19:38,734
Yes, when the country...

478
00:19:38,734 --> 00:19:39,734
Of course.

479
00:19:39,734 --> 00:19:40,734
Right.

480
00:19:42,734 --> 00:19:48,734
You're saying that I'm living totally reactively.

481
00:19:48,734 --> 00:19:51,734
No, you're totally living in a kind of...

482
00:19:51,734 --> 00:19:52,734
What?

483
00:19:52,734 --> 00:19:55,734
Miasma, confusion.

484
00:19:55,734 --> 00:19:57,734
From one piece to the next.

485
00:19:57,734 --> 00:19:58,734
Yes.

486
00:19:58,734 --> 00:20:00,734
From one reaction to the next reaction.

487
00:20:00,734 --> 00:20:03,734
Reward and punishment in that movement.

488
00:20:03,734 --> 00:20:06,734
Right.

489
00:20:06,734 --> 00:20:11,734
So can we be aware actually now...

490
00:20:11,734 --> 00:20:12,734
Mm-hmm.

491
00:20:12,734 --> 00:20:20,734
Of the various fragments?

492
00:20:20,734 --> 00:20:26,233
That I am a Hindu, that I am a Jew, that I am an Arab, that I am a communist, that I

493
00:20:26,233 --> 00:20:31,733
am a Catholic, that I am a businessman, I am married, I have responsibilities, I am an artist, I am a scientist.

494
00:20:31,733 --> 00:20:32,733
You follow?

495
00:20:32,733 --> 00:20:37,733
These various sociological fragmentations.

496
00:20:37,733 --> 00:20:38,733
Right.

497
00:20:38,733 --> 00:20:40,733
As well as psychological fragmentations.

498
00:20:40,733 --> 00:20:41,733
Right.

499
00:20:41,734 --> 00:20:43,734
That's exactly what I started with.

500
00:20:43,734 --> 00:20:44,734
Right.

501
00:20:44,734 --> 00:20:48,234
This feeling that I am a fragment, this feeling

502
00:20:48,234 --> 00:20:51,734
that that's where I get absorbed, is being a fragment.

503
00:20:51,734 --> 00:20:53,734
Which you call the individual.

504
00:20:53,734 --> 00:20:55,734
That I call important.

505
00:20:55,734 --> 00:20:56,734
Not just the individual.

506
00:20:56,734 --> 00:20:57,734
You call that important.

507
00:20:57,734 --> 00:20:58,734
Right.

508
00:20:58,734 --> 00:21:00,734
That I have to work.

509
00:21:00,734 --> 00:21:01,734
Quite.

510
00:21:01,734 --> 00:21:04,734
See, that it's significant.

511
00:21:04,734 --> 00:21:07,734
So can we now, in talking over together, be

512
00:21:07,734 --> 00:21:10,734
aware of the fact that we are all human beings?

513
00:21:10,734 --> 00:21:11,734
Together.

514
00:21:11,734 --> 00:21:14,734
Be aware that I am that.

515
00:21:14,734 --> 00:21:16,734
Mm-hmm.

516
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:23,234
I am a fragment, and therefore creating more fragments, more conflict, more

517
00:21:23,234 --> 00:21:29,734
misery, more confusion, more sorrow, because when there is conflict, it affects everything.

518
00:21:29,734 --> 00:21:31,734
Right.

519
00:21:31,734 --> 00:21:33,734
Can you be aware of

520
00:21:33,734 --> 00:21:35,734
it as we are discussing it?

521
00:21:35,734 --> 00:21:38,734
Mm-hmm.

522
00:21:38,734 --> 00:21:40,234
I can be aware as

523
00:21:40,234 --> 00:21:41,734
we are discussing it a little.

524
00:21:41,734 --> 00:21:42,734
Not a little.

525
00:21:42,734 --> 00:21:43,734
I don't know about that.

526
00:21:43,734 --> 00:21:44,734
A little.

527
00:21:44,734 --> 00:21:45,734
That's the trouble.

528
00:21:45,734 --> 00:21:50,734
Why can't I be aware of it?

529
00:21:50,734 --> 00:21:52,734
No, sir.

530
00:21:52,734 --> 00:21:55,734
You are only aware of it when there is conflict.

531
00:21:55,734 --> 00:21:57,734
It is not a conflict in you now.

532
00:21:57,734 --> 00:21:58,734
Yes.

533
00:21:58,734 --> 00:22:00,234
But is it possible to

534
00:22:00,234 --> 00:22:01,734
be aware of it without conflict?

535
00:22:01,734 --> 00:22:03,734
That's the next thing, yes.

536
00:22:03,734 --> 00:22:06,734
That requires quite a different approach.

537
00:22:06,734 --> 00:22:08,734
Well, how will we consider this different?

538
00:22:08,734 --> 00:22:09,734
Quite a different approach.

539
00:22:09,734 --> 00:22:10,734
Mm-hmm.

540
00:22:10,734 --> 00:22:11,734
Quite a different approach.

541
00:22:11,734 --> 00:22:12,734
Mm-hmm.

542
00:22:12,734 --> 00:22:17,734
But I was thinking of looking at one point that the importance of these fragments is that

543
00:22:17,734 --> 00:22:22,734
when I identify myself and say, I am this, I am that, I mean the whole of me.

544
00:22:22,734 --> 00:22:25,234
In other words, I am the whole of

545
00:22:25,234 --> 00:22:27,734
me is rich or poor or American or whatever.

546
00:22:27,734 --> 00:22:28,734
